{"format":"tvf-scene","v":1,"name":"example · reading and writing","loop":44,"ease":"","hold":0,"gravity":1,"wind":0,"trail":null,"camera":[{"t":0,"box":[-0.3096,-0.180126,0.0036,0.0972]},{"t":0.23,"box":[-0.3096,-0.180126,0.0036,0.0972]},{"t":0.28,"box":[-0.3195,-0.182826,0.1341,0.208251]},{"t":0.33,"box":[-0.3195,-0.182826,0.1341,0.208251]},{"t":0.37,"box":[-0.3096,-0.180126,0.0036,0.0972]},{"t":0.82,"box":[-0.3096,-0.180126,0.0036,0.0972]},{"t":0.88,"box":[-0.3195,-0.182826,0.1341,0.208251]}],"stops":[0.2,0.4,0.6,0.78],"beats":[{"title":"From one place, directions only","text":"Stand in a room's corner and look round. Each thing comes to you as a direction: a ray from where you stand. That is a **reading**, a ratio of two lengths, and it costs nothing.\n\nWhat it does not give is how far. A room half the size, with everything in it half as far, sends every ray the same way: the faint copy lies on the very same rays."},{"title":"Scale the world","text":"The test is simple. Make everything bigger by the same factor: the room, its things, you, your stride. Every ray keeps its direction. **Nothing a reading holds can change**, because a reading is a ratio of two lengths that both grew.\n\nWhatever does change under this test is not a reading. [The test, §5](https://github.com/reportbase/wander/blob/main/papers/essays/01-reading-and-writing.md)"},{"title":"One step","text":"Walk one step along the wall, a direction you know, and look again. From the new place each thing gives a second ray, and the two rays cross at the thing. Every thing now has a **place**, and the room a shape, all in steps: it is 3.57 steps wide.\n\nStill no metres. The step is the unit, and how long a step is, no reading says."},{"title":"Count the stride","text":"To say how big, something has to be carried in: count the step as six strides of 0.7 m. That one amount, 4.2 m, **writes** every length in the room: it is 15.0 m wide.\n\nThis is the only part that was not free. A writing costs an amount brought from outside the readings. [What writing costs, §6](https://github.com/reportbase/wander/blob/main/papers/essays/01-reading-and-writing.md)"},{"title":"Scale the world again","text":"Now scale everything once more. The rays and the places in steps stay where they were; the room is still 3.57 steps wide. But the step is now 6.3 m and the room 22.5 m: **the metres moved, and only the metres**.\n\nThat is the whole line between the two. A reading is unchanged when the world is scaled; a writing changes with it, and needs one amount from outside to be made at all."}],"path":null,"items":[{"fill":{"color":"#f4f1ea","opacity":1},"stroke":null,"width":0,"open":false,"exact":{"x":[-0.9,0.9,0.9,-0.9],"y":[0.63,0.63,-0.63,-0.63],"r":null,"smooth":null,"ctrl":null,"holes":[]}},{"morph":0},{"morph":1},{"morph":2},{"morph":3},{"morph":6},{"morph":7},{"morph":8},{"morph":9},{"morph":10},{"morph":11},{"morph":12},{"morph":13},{"morph":4},{"morph":15},{"morph":16},{"morph":18},{"morph":19},{"morph":20},{"morph":21},{"morph":22},{"morph":23},{"morph":24},{"morph":25},{"morph":27},{"morph":28},{"morph":29},{"morph":30},{"morph":31},{"morph":32},{"morph":33},{"morph":5},{"morph":17},{"morph":14},{"morph":35},{"morph":36},{"morph":37},{"morph":34},{"morph":90},{"morph":91},{"morph":92},{"morph":38},{"morph":39},{"morph":40},{"morph":41},{"morph":42},{"morph":43},{"morph":44},{"morph":45},{"morph":46},{"morph":47},{"morph":48},{"morph":49},{"morph":50},{"morph":51},{"morph":52},{"morph":53},{"morph":54},{"morph":55},{"morph":56},{"morph":57},{"morph":58},{"morph":59},{"morph":60},{"morph":61},{"morph":26},{"morph":62},{"morph":63},{"morph":64},{"morph":65},{"morph":66},{"morph":67},{"morph":68},{"morph":69},{"morph":70},{"morph":71},{"morph":72},{"morph":73},{"morph":74},{"morph":75},{"morph":76},{"morph":77},{"morph":78},{"morph":79},{"morph":80},{"morph":81},{"morph":82},{"morph":83},{"morph":84},{"morph":85},{"morph":86},{"morph":87},{"morph":88},{"morph":89}],"morphs":[{"ex